/**
 * Traced fashion-plate line art. Every garment the dress code section draws is
 * one of these; there is no second drawing language.
 *
 * ## Provenance
 *
 * Two line drawings supplied by the organizer, each a couple standing together:
 * a gown beside a dinner suit, and a sari-and-sbai drape beside a mandarin-collar
 * tunic suit. Both arrived as SVGs whose payload was actually a raster image
 * behind an alpha mask — nothing a stylesheet could recolour. Each mask was
 * thresholded, its ink boundary walked into closed rings, and each ring
 * simplified (Douglas-Peucker, epsilon 1.8px of the ~810x1150 original) into the
 * paths below. Both sets were traced with identical settings, which is what
 * keeps the two families in one hand: a coarser epsilon on the traditional set
 * would have saved 5KB and made it visibly the cruder drawing of the two.
 *
 * ## These are outlines, not strokes
 *
 * The tracer follows the *edge* of every drawn line, so one pen stroke becomes a
 * long closed ring around it. That is why these render as `fill` with
 * `fill-rule: evenodd` and never as `stroke`: filling the ring paints the
 * line, evenodd knocks the enclosed areas back out. It also means the line
 * weight is baked into the geometry — it scales with the figure instead of
 * staying a constant hairline, which is what a fashion plate does and what a
 * stroked icon cannot.
 *
 * ## Why a couple path and not two solo ones side by side
 *
 * Each family carries three paths, and the COUPLE is not its two solo figures
 * placed next to each other. A solo path is normalised to fill its own 100x100
 * box, because a lone figure should use the frame it is given; that independent
 * scaling throws away the fact that the dinner suit is shorter than a
 * floor-length gown, and that the tunic ends well above the drape's sweep. The
 * couple paths keep the illustrator's original composition — the true height
 * relationship, the slight overlap — so a code that applies to everyone reads as
 * one drawing rather than two icons pushed together.
 *
 * Coordinates carry one decimal. At 200px, one decimal and two are
 * indistinguishable, and it is the difference between 15KB and 18KB.
 */

export const GARMENT_ART_VIEWBOX = '0 0 100 100'

